{"tool_name":"chromosight","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"chromosight","identifiers":[],"license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Detect loops (and other patterns) in hi-c contact maps.","home_url":"https://github.com/koszullab/chromosight","keywords":["Genomics"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":69},"biotools":{"id":"chromosight","home":"https://github.com/koszullab/chromosight","summary":"Chromosight is an algorithm inspired from computer vision that can detect patterns in Hi-C maps. Chromosight has greater sensitivity than existing methods, while being faster and applicable to any type of genomes, including bacteria, viruses, yeasts and mammals.","addition_date":"2021-01-18T08:13:54Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:34:48.882890Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:chromosight","credit":[{"email":"cyril.mattheydoret@gmail.com","name":"Cyril Matthey-Doret","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1126-1535","rorid":"02hdt9m26","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer"]},{"email":"acournac@pasteur.fr","name":"Axel Cournac","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"rkoszul@pasteur.fr","name":"Romain Koszul","typeEntity":"Person"}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://chromosight.readthedocs.io/en/latest/"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Structural distance matrix","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2856"},"format":[{"term":"HDF5","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3590"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Enrichment analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3501"},{"term":"Mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2429"},{"term":"Peak calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3222"},{"term":"Standardisation and normalisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3435"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Statistical estimate score","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0951"},"format":[{"term":"TSV","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3475"}]}]}],"name":"Chromosight","owner":"cmdoret","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/s41467-020-19562-7","metadata":{"abstract":"Chromosomes of all species studied so far display a variety of higher-order organisational features, such as self-interacting domains or loops. These structures, which are often associated to biological functions, form distinct, visible patterns on genome-wide contact maps generated by chromosome conformation capture approaches such as Hi-C. Here we present Chromosight, an algorithm inspired from computer vision that can detect patterns in contact maps. Chromosight has greater sensitivity than existing methods on synthetic simulated data, while being faster and applicable to any type of genomes, including bacteria, viruses, yeasts and mammals. Our method does not require any prior training dataset and works well with default parameters on data generated with various protocols.","authors":[{"name":"Baudry L."},{"name":"Breuer A."},{"name":"Campeas A."},{"name":"Chanut P.H."},{"name":"Cournac A."},{"name":"Guiglielmoni N."},{"name":"Jean E."},{"name":"Koszul R."},{"name":"Matthey-Doret C."},{"name":"Meot A."},{"name":"Montagne R."},{"name":"Moreau P."},{"name":"Oriol E."},{"name":"Politis L."},{"name":"Scolari V."},{"name":"Vigouroux A."}],"citationCount":54,"date":"2020-12-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nature Communications","title":"Computer vision for pattern detection in chromosome contact maps"},"pmcid":"PMC7670471","pmid":"33199682","type":["Primary"]},{"doi":"10.1101/2020.03.08.981910","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"DNA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0654"},{"term":"Data mining","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3473"},{"term":"Mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0102"},{"term":"Model organisms","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0621"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"Chromosight","home":"https://bio.tools/chromosight","summary":"Chromosight is an algorithm inspired from compute